@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `il07-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-credit-points-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-s33a-credit-point`
IMPORT `ito-s34-s36-s36a-credits`
IMPORT `ito-credit-points-published-figures`

-- ===========================================================================
-- IL-07 adapter for row IL-01: Income Tax Ordinance ss 33A, 34, 36, 36A.
--
-- This module imports this row's nouns and IL-01's modules (vendored copies,
-- VENDORED.sha256) and nothing of any other row, so every IL-01 name it uses
-- resolves to IL-01 alone. It exposes plain numbers, under names that begin
-- "IL-01:". It decides nothing of its own: each rule below hands the household's
-- facts to an IL-01 rule and returns its answer.
--
-- VERSION 0.3.0 (2026-10-08, BACKLOG IL-22). Row IL-01's version 0.2.0 takes the
-- tax year (its repair 01-YR: each section's rules refuse a year before its last
-- listed amendment) and s 3A(f) (01-S09: an Israeli citizen who is a resident of
-- the Area, or operates in it, is treated as an Israeli resident), in a new
-- record, `Taxpayer in a tax year`. The pipeline now calls the forms below whose
-- names end "in tax year"; the forms without it, which call IL-01's year-free
-- rules, are kept for the tests of this adapter.
-- INPUT CONVENTION (s 3A(f)): the household holds one residence fact under the
-- Ordinance, `the earner was an Israeli resident in the tax year, under the Income
-- Tax Ordinance`, and no s 3A(f) fact. The capstone gives IL-01 both s 3A(f)
-- facts as FALSE and answers on residence as its caller gives it: a caller whose
-- earner is an Israeli citizen resident in the Area, or operating there, whom
-- s 3A(f) treats "as if" an Israeli resident, gives TRUE in that field, as the
-- Ordinance itself does. (Assumed, not ruled: the lead's direction for IL-22.)
--
-- VERSION 0.5.0 (2026-10-08, BACKLOG IL-54). Row IL-01's version 0.3.0 (SHRUG,
-- its forks F2 and F4) adds two facts to `Taxpayer in a tax year`. INPUT
-- CONVENTIONS (assumed, not ruled: the lead's direction for IL-54):
-- * income from personal exertion in the tax year: the earner's only income is
--   the salary, paid in every month of the year the capstone answers (fork K1),
--   and a salary from employment is income from personal exertion, so the fact
--   is whether the monthly salary is above nil;
-- * residence over the tax year: the household holds one residence fact for the
--   tax year, so it is given as holding for the whole tax year. An earner who
--   was an Israeli resident for only part of it is outside what the household
--   can state.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `IL-07 adapter — row IL-01`

§§ `The earner, as IL-01's Person`

-- IL-01's `Individual` carries four facts; the earner record carries each under
-- its own name. IL-01's `a woman` is a BOOLEAN field here, where row IL-02 has a
-- constructor of the same name (RECONCILE.md, clash N2).
GIVEN e IS AN `IL-07 earner`
GIVETH A Person
`IL-01: the earner as a person` e MEANS
    `an individual`
        (Individual WITH
            `an Israeli resident in the tax year`                  IS e's `the earner was an Israeli resident in the tax year, under the Income Tax Ordinance`
            `a woman`                                              IS e's `the earner is a woman`
            `a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen` IS e's `the earner is a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen`
            `a foreign worker`                                     IS e's `the earner is a foreign worker`)

§§ `The earner, as IL-01's taxpayer in a tax year (version 0.3.0)`

@ref ITO s 3A(f), line 471 (row IL-01, ito-credit-points-nouns.l4); s 1 "הכנסה מיגיעה אישית" and ss 34, 36 (row IL-01 v0.3.0, forks F2 and F4); the input conventions above
GIVEN e          IS AN `IL-07 earner`
      `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Taxpayer in a tax year`
`IL-01: the earner` e `as a taxpayer in tax year` `the year` MEANS
    `Taxpayer in a tax year` WITH
        `the taxpayer`                                     IS `IL-01: the earner as a person` e
        `the tax year`                                     IS `the year`
        `an Israeli citizen who is a resident of the Area` IS FALSE
        `an Israeli citizen who operates in the Area`      IS FALSE
        `the taxpayer had income from personal exertion in the tax year` IS e's `the earner's monthly salary` GREATER THAN 0
        `the taxpayer's Israeli residence over the tax year`             IS `the residence entered held for the whole tax year`

§§ `The credit points`

@ref ITO ss 34, 36 and 36A (row IL-01, ito-s34-s36-s36a-credits.l4)
GIVEN e IS AN `IL-07 earner`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`IL-01: the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A for the earner` e MEANS
    `the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A for` (`IL-01: the earner as a person` e)

@ref ITO s 36A (row IL-01, ito-s34-s36-s36a-credits.l4)
GIVEN e IS AN `IL-07 earner`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`IL-01: the credit points under section 36A for the earner` e MEANS
    `the credit points under section 36A for` (`IL-01: the earner as a person` e)

-- Version 0.3.0: the same, for a tax year (IL-01's year-aware rules).
@ref ITO ss 34, 36 and 36A, for a tax year (row IL-01 v0.2.0, ito-s34-s36-s36a-credits.l4)
GIVEN e          IS AN `IL-07 earner`
      `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`IL-01: the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A for the earner` e `in tax year` `the year` MEANS
    `the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A in the tax year of` (`IL-01: the earner` e `as a taxpayer in tax year` `the year`)

@ref ITO s 36A, for a tax year (row IL-01 v0.2.0, ito-s34-s36-s36a-credits.l4)
GIVEN e          IS AN `IL-07 earner`
      `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`IL-01: the credit points under section 36A for the earner` e `in tax year` `the year` MEANS
    `the credit points under section 36A in the tax year of` (`IL-01: the earner` e `as a taxpayer in tax year` `the year`)

-- Version 0.5.0: row IL-01's readings of its forks F1, F2 and F4 (its v0.3.0,
-- SHRUG), with F1 as the capstone's reading of s 36A names it and F2 and F4 at
-- row IL-01's own switches. Under the input conventions above, F2 parts only for
-- an earner with no salary and F4 never.
@ref ITO ss 34, 36, 36A (row IL-01 v0.3.0, ito-credit-points-nouns.l4 and ito-s34-s36-s36a-credits.l4, forks F1, F2, F4)
GIVEN x IS AN `IL-07 a reading of section 36A on residence`
GIVETH A `The readings of forks F1, F2 and F4`
`IL-01: its readings, with section 36A read as` x MEANS
    `The readings of forks F1, F2 and F4` WITH
        `fork F1, section 36A and residence`                    IS
            CONSIDER x
            WHEN `IL-07: section 36A at the rows' own switches, declined where residence decides it` THEN `section 36A — the reading this row takes on residence`
            WHEN `IL-07: section 36A without a residence condition`                                  THEN `section 36A has no residence condition`
            WHEN `IL-07: section 36A only for an Israeli resident`                                   THEN `section 36A gives its half point only to an Israeli resident`
        `fork F2, section 36 and income from personal exertion` IS `section 36 — the reading this row takes on income from personal exertion`
        `fork F4, residence for part of a tax year`             IS `sections 34 and 36 — the reading this row takes for part of a tax year`

@ref ITO ss 34, 36 and 36A, for a tax year (row IL-01 v0.3.0, ito-s34-s36-s36a-credits.l4, forks F1, F2, F4)
GIVEN e          IS AN `IL-07 earner`
      `the year` IS A NUMBER
      x          IS AN `IL-07 a reading of section 36A on residence`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`IL-01: the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A for the earner` e `in tax year` `the year` `, reading section 36A as` x MEANS
    `the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A in the tax year of` (`IL-01: the earner` e `as a taxpayer in tax year` `the year`)
        `, under the readings` (`IL-01: its readings, with section 36A read as` x)

§§ `Section 33A — points to money, and the set-off`

@ref ITO s 33A "נקודת זיכוי", limbs (1)-(2) (row IL-01, ito-s33a-credit-point.l4)
GIVEN `the points` IS A NUMBER
      `the value`  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`IL-01: the amount of` `the points` `credit points at a value of` `the value` MEANS
    `the amount of` `the points` `credit points at a credit-point value of` `the value`

@ref ITO s 33A "נקודת זיכוי", limb (3) (row IL-01, ito-s33a-credit-point.l4; IL-01 fork F5)
GIVEN `the credit` IS A NUMBER
      `the tax`    IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`IL-01: the tax after setting off` `the credit` `against` `the tax` MEANS
    `the tax for the year after setting off` `the credit` `against` `the tax`

-- Version 0.3.0: the same two, for a tax year (s 33A's text from tax year 2005).
@ref ITO s 33A "נקודת זיכוי", limbs (1)-(2), for a tax year (row IL-01 v0.2.0, ito-s33a-credit-point.l4)
GIVEN `the points` IS A NUMBER
      `the value`  IS A NUMBER
      `the year`   IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`IL-01: the amount of` `the points` `credit points at a value of` `the value` `in tax year` `the year` MEANS
    `the amount of` `the points` `credit points at a credit-point value of` `the value` `in tax year` `the year`

@ref ITO s 33A "נקודת זיכוי", limb (3), for a tax year (row IL-01 v0.2.0, ito-s33a-credit-point.l4; IL-01 fork F5)
GIVEN `the credit` IS A NUMBER
      `the tax`    IS A NUMBER
      `the year`   IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`IL-01: the tax after setting off` `the credit` `against` `the tax` `in tax year` `the year` MEANS
    `the tax for the year after setting off` `the credit` `against` `the tax` `in tax year` `the year`

§§ `Figures IL-01 sourced from the Israel Tax Authority (not law)`

-- [itc135-2025] p. 4: the value of a credit point in tax year 2025 is NIS 2,904
-- (IL-01 NOTES.md section 4; ito-credit-points-published-figures.l4).
@ref Israel Tax Authority, form 135 notes for 2025, p. 4 (row IL-01, sha256 207412d9...ad0eb)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`IL-01: the value of one credit point the Israel Tax Authority published for tax year 2025` MEANS
    `the value of one credit point published by the Israel Tax Authority for tax year` 2025

-- The withholding booklet's monthly figure (IL-01 NOTES.md section 4): 242 for
-- 2024, 2025 and 2026; refused for any other year.
@ref Israel Tax Authority, monthly withholding booklets 2024-2026 (row IL-01)
GIVEN `the tax year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`IL-01: the monthly credit-point figure in the withholding booklet for tax year` `the tax year` MEANS
    `the monthly credit-point figure in the Israel Tax Authority's withholding booklet for tax year` `the tax year`
